1ow4|n|The act of referring, or the state of being referred; as, reference to a chart for guidance. ; That which refers to something; a specific direction of the attention; as, a reference in a text-book. ; Relation; regard; respect. ; One who, or that which, is referred to. ; One of whom inquires can be made as to the integrity, capacity, and the like, of another. ; A work, or a passage in a work, to which one is referred. ; The act of submitting a matter in dispute to the judgment of one or more persons for decision. ; The process of sending any matter, for inquiry in a cause, to a master or other officer, in order that he may ascertain facts and report to the court. ; Appeal.	a:7ig,64,32;7ih,61,4;1ghq,57,7;5kz,56,60;7i9,54,3;cwr,54,6;6fk,53,4;s67,51,2;16ev,47,7;1ddm,45,5;27jb,43,214;x96,39,5;1ddv,38,5;y0m,38,38;21fw,37,9~12l0,28,239;27jb,43,214;26ej,18,126;ugg,15,121;5kz,56,60;1yel,19,60;13x9,12,50;qfc,32,43;210p,15,40;y0m,38,38;1cf9,5,36;1p9l,5,34;7ig,64,32;1p9p,18,29;wph,27,24	v:1ykh,41,3;v40,32,4;39h,26,3;l8n,21,2;1t7,21,7;6gd,18,123;1pr0,15,6;mab,14,1;1v4q,13,3;cwx,10,10;gc,9,2;1ta,9,1;x0w,9,7;gb,9,3;ffd,8,8~6gd,18,123;mu8,6,48;cwx,10,10;ffd,8,8;1gqb,3,7;1t7,21,7;x0w,9,7;1pr0,15,6;1r2j,6,5;1dhn,0,4;v40,32,4;17k5,4,3;1ykh,41,3;39h,26,3;gb,9,3	V:gk3,41,2;10i6,30,3;1ykg,28,97;epq,28,6;1t7,24,9;17sg,21,104;da3,19,3;1u5l,16,14;w4n,16,3;cyo,14,3;g7i,14,5;725,11,1;17sl,11,4;27ir,9,7;j9r,9,5~17sg,21,104;1ykg,28,97;1u5l,16,14;1t7,24,9;27ir,9,7;epq,28,6;cwy,8,6;g7i,14,5;27hi,2,5;1zms,4,5;j9r,9,5;1nql,7,5;17sl,11,4;1dhp,7,4;10i6,30,3	n:10cv,52,4;wd1,43,6;4zb,43,69;f6z,42,127;1kod,41,3;sn0,38,9;5ki,36,3;27pj,36,182;7ij,35,8;kaw,33,4;1xii,31,9;1ijl,30,3;27ph,29,5;go9,27,3;wo4,23,4~27pj,36,182;f6z,42,127;4zb,43,69;jlq,22,59;oq5,7,39;cwu,23,29;16f1,18,24;5ea,22,18;yfc,18,15;d1i,11,14;sn0,38,9;47b,6,9;1xii,31,9;4e6,1,8;7ij,35,8	N:jbh,95,271;hto,76,30;160x,58,17;wo4,56,40;p24,52,38;nib,48,3;13pa,47,3;jbf,47,19;39j,47,28;27pj,44,323;1toh,42,286;4z9,40,5;ndq,39,3;1ro7,32,7;4zb,