1p8p|n|To make lax or loose; to make less close, firm, rigid, tense, or the like; to slacken; to loosen; to open; as, to relax a rope or cord; to relax the muscles or sinews. ; To make less severe or rigorous; to abate the stringency of; to remit in respect to strenuousness, earnestness, or effort; as, to relax discipline; to relax one's attention or endeavors. ; Hence, to relieve from attention or effort; to ease; to recreate; to divert; as, amusement relaxes the mind. ; To relieve from constipation; to loosen; to open; as, an aperient relaxes the bowels. ; Relaxation.	n:1bhf,47,2~1bhf,47,2
