1q9m|n|The act of returning, or coming back; return. ; That which reverts or returns; residue. ; The returning of an esttate to the grantor or his heirs, by operation of law, after the grant has terminated; hence, the residue of an estate left in the proprietor or owner thereof, to take effect in possession, by operation of law, after the termination of a limited or less estate carved out of it and conveyed by him. ; Hence, a right to future possession or enjoiment; succession. ; A payment which is not to be received, or a benefit which does not begin, until the happening of some event, as the death of a living person. ; A return towards some ancestral type or character; atavism.	a:17zj,93,67~17zj,93,67	n:1abn,28,4~1abn,28,4	N:ak6,80,4;1abn,31,5~1abn,31,5;ak6,80,4
